From b8fa76e395d10aebcd80d70af5bf510641f2a7e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:51:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] session list: test plain columns before the
 model_config JSON lineage clauses; index the pinned back-fill

Every state.db write changes the sidebar cache key, so the Desktop's next poll rebuilds the
three sidebar slices with list_sessions_rich. Two costs per rebuild:

- _session_filter_where emitted the child-lineage clauses (_LISTABLE_CHILD_SQL and the
  _delegate_from json_extract) before s.source NOT IN / s.message_count / s.archived, so
  every sessions row paid json_valid + json_extract before the cheap column tests rejected
  it. The plain-column clauses now come first and the lineage clauses last. The lineage
  clauses bind no parameters, so the parameter list is unchanged.
- The pinned back-fill's `SELECT id FROM sessions WHERE pinned = 1` was a full sessions
  scan, once per slice. New partial index idx_sessions_pinned ON sessions(pinned, id)
  WHERE pinned = 1, declared in DEFERRED_INDEX_SQL beside idx_sessions_effective_activity,
  so an existing store gets it on its next writable open (no schema-version bump). With
  (id) alone the planner still walked the index (`SCAN sessions USING COVERING INDEX`);
  leading with pinned makes it a SEARCH (pinned=?).

Rows, counts and order are unchanged (differential dump of 85 list_sessions_rich /
session_count variants on a fixture with roots, branch, reset, compression, delegate,
pinned+archived and hidden rows: byte-identical parent vs change).

Synthetic fixture (11,000 sessions, 70% kanban, every row a model_config object, 2 pins),
median process_time of the three sidebar slices, parent -> change (rounds 2-4):
24.5/25.1/23.7 ms -> 17.9/16.1/15.7 ms.

Tests: tests/hermes_state/test_session_filter_clause_order.py (RED on parent, GREEN here).
Fixture maintenance: tests/hermes_cli/test_browse_schema_drift.py::_drop_session_column also
drops idx_sessions_pinned before DROP COLUMN pinned (as it already does for
idx_sessions_effective_activity); no row/count/order assertion changed. No existing test
pinned the old clause order as text.
